General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:61:| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-62-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-63-## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-64-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-65-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-66-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:67:| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-68-| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-70-| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-72-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-73-## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-74-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-75-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-76-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event