review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:111:complete lowering or approximation policy is not.\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:164:### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:192:### G7. Standards, banks and insurance are largely deferred requirements\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:218:### G8. Literature breadth exceeds the depth of the follow-up screening\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:246:### G9. Tool selection is a shortlist, without demonstrated adapter contracts\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:265:### G10. Acceptance and completion are not yet determinate\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:289:## Prioritised repair sequence\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:306:## Review evidence and limits\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:320:that any proposed library is unsuitable.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:1:# Review against the AccDSL mission\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:9:## Answer and review scope\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:24:## Goals and current coverage\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:37:## Additional explicit findings\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:39:### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:41:Requirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:121:Requirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:147:avoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:156:### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:158:Requirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:174:### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:176:Requirements: MC25, MC34. Refines G2, G9 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:193:## Completion consequences\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:213:## Evidence and limits of this pass\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:1:# Active checkpoint\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:8:## Accepted source corpus and next execution\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:38:Core 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:46:## Current deliverable\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:83:## Evidence preserved\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:99:manifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:105:compiler. The new `core_semantics.py` validates the authored monetary debt\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:117:## Remaining work and next justified steps\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:119:1. Extend the checked debt-profile registry/reference/type validation and implement source-to-IR lowering\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:120:   against the positive/negative cases. Schema parsing is not complete compiler\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:146:## Recovery history\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/humanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
