{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '420,501p' scripts/core_semantics.py; cat docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json\"","aggregated_output":"                    self.assumption(fields[name], c['id'])\n        for s in d['states']:\n            self.ref(s['book'], {'books'}); iso_date(s['date'], s['id'])\n            seen = set(); total = Fraction(0)\n            for b in s['balances']:\n                a = self.ref(b['account'], {'accounts'})\n                require(a['book'] == s['book'], 'StateBook', s['id'], 'Balance belongs to another book')\n                require(a['id'] not in seen, 'DuplicateBalance', s['id'], a['id']); seen.add(a['id'])\n                total += rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id'])\n            require(total == 0, 'UnbalancedState', s['id'], 'Signed opening balances must sum to zero')\n            require(seen == {a['id'] for a in d['accounts'] if a['book'] == s['book']}, 'IncompleteState', s['id'], 'This fixture requires explicit zero balances too')\n            self.refs(s['contracts'], {'contracts'}); self.refs(s['dependencies'])\n            require(not s['measurements'], 'UnsupportedState', s['id'], 'Measurement state not validated in this profile')\n            require(all(self.nodes[c]['book'] == s['book'] for c in s['contracts']),\n                    'StateBook', s['id'], 'Active contract belongs to another book')\n            opening = package_data['registry']['after-2025-close']\n            require(s['book'] == opening['book'] and s['date'] == opening['date'] and\n                    set(s['contracts']) == set(opening['contracts']) and\n                    {b['account']: rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id']) for b in s['balances']} ==\n                    {a: Fraction(v) for a, v in opening['signed_balances'].items()},\n                    'OpeningStateMismatch', s['id'], 'Balanced state differs from the frozen authored opening')\n        for s in d['scenarios']:\n            require(s['kind'] == 'ExogenousStress' and s['probability_model'] is None and s['observed_event'] is None and s['structural_model'] is None and not s['replaced_equations'], 'UnsupportedScenario', s['id'], 'Exogenous debt stress only')\n            require(len(s['drivers']) == 1 and s['drivers'][0]['name'] == 'market_rate', 'ScenarioDrivers', s['id'], 'Expected market_rate')\n            require(self.expression(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])[0] == 'Driver<Rate<annual_simple>>', 'TypeMismatch', s['id'], 'Rate driver required')\n            self.assumption(s['drivers'][0]['expression'], s['id'])\n            low, _ = self.bounds(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])\n            require(low is not None and low >= 0, 'ContractDomain', s['id'], 'DemoDebt rejects a negative reset rate')\n        for scope in d['modelScopes']:\n            self.refs(scope['templates'], {'ContractType'}); self.refs(scope['calendars'], {'Calendar'})\n            require(not scope['choices'] and not scope['obligations'], 'UnsupportedScope', scope['id'], 'Additional structural choices/obligations need a fuller checker')\n            require(len(scope['slot_limits']) == 1, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'One concrete debt slot limit required')\n            for slot in scope['slot_limits']:\n                require(self.expression(slot['expression'])[0] == 'Int', 'SlotLimitType', scope['id'], 'Slot limit is an integer, not an implicit Real cast')\n                low, high = self.bounds(slot['expression'])\n                require(low == high and low is not None and low >= 0 and slot['name'] == 'debt_contracts' and len(d['contracts']) <= low, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'Concrete nonnegative capacity required')\n        for f in d['historyFamilies']:\n            for key, kind in [('scope', 'modelScopes'), ('evidence_view', 'evidenceViews'), ('opening_state', 'states')]:\n                self.ref(f[key], {kind})\n            for key, kind in [('symbols', 'symbols'), ('constraints', 'constraints'), ('alternatives', 'alternatives')]:\n                self.refs(f[key], {kind})\n            self.refs(f['witnesses'], {'Witness'}); self.refs(f['solver_results'], {'ReferenceResult'})\n            view = self.nodes[f['evidence_view']]\n            require(all(o['id'] in view['observations'] for o in d['observations']) and\n                    all(s['admission'] in view['decisions'] for s in d['symbols']),\n                    'ViewMembership', f['id'], 'All evidence used by this bounded family must be selected')\n            require(set(f['symbols']) == {s['id'] for s in d['symbols']} and\n                    set(f['alternatives']) == {a['id'] for a in d['alternatives'] if a['parent'] == f['id']},\n                    'FamilyMembership', f['id'], 'Family omits an authored symbol or conditional alternative')\n            require(not f['choices'], 'UnsupportedChoice', f['id'], 'Finite structural cells not implemented here')\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or f['unresolved_cells'] == 0, 'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact coverage cannot contain unknown cells')\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or (f['completed_cells'] > 0 and f['solver_results']),\n                    'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact label needs completed cells and result references; this is not proof verification')\n            require(f['feasibility'] != 'Feasible' or bool(f['witnesses']), 'MissingWitness', f['id'], 'Feasible label requires a witness reference')\n        for r in d['reportMappings']:\n            b = self.ref(r['book'], {'books'})\n            require(r['basis'] == b['basis'], 'PackageBasis', r['id'], 'Report and book bases differ')\n            self.ref(r['closing_policy'], {'Operation'}); self.ref(r['cash_flow_policy'], {'CashFlowPolicy'})\n            self.refs(r['required_operations'], {'Operation'})\n            require(r['closing_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/close' and r['cash_flow_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/interest_operating'\n                    and r['required_operations'] == ['DemoDebt@1/accrue_and_pay'], 'ReportPolicy', r['id'],\n                    'Wrong policy binding for the frozen report template')\n            require(len(r['rows']) == 1 and r['rows'][0]['name'] == 'package_mapping', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'One frozen template binding required')\n            for row in r['rows']:\n                require(self.expression(row['expression'])[0] == 'SourceRef', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'This profile binds a frozen report template')\n                e = self.nodes[row['expression']]\n                require(e['op'] == 'literal' and e['text'] == 'DemoDebt.statements.v1', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'Expected the statement mapping export')\n        for m in d['models']:\n            self.refs(m['declarations']); self.refs(m['package_lock'], {'packages'}); self.ref(m['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\n            require(m['language_version'] == 'Core0.1', 'UnsupportedLanguage', m['id'], 'Core0.1 only')\n            required = {r['id'] for section in ['entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'observations', 'symbols',\n                        'contracts', 'alternatives', 'scenarios', 'reportMappings', 'states'] for r in d[section]}\n            require(required <= set(m['declarations']) and set(m['package_lock']) == {p['id'] for p in d['packages']},\n                    'ModelMembership', m['id'], 'Model omits an authored declaration or package lock')\n        return {'status': 'passed', 'profile': 'authored-debt-example',\n                'internal_records': len(self.nodes), 'external_exports': len(self.external),\n                'coverage_claims_verified': False,\n                'limits': 'Bounded static admission only; no general compiler, runtime, accounting certification or proof of historical coverage.'}\n\n\ndef validate(document, registry, schema, root):\n    return Validator(document, registry, schema, root).validate()\n{\n  \"id\": \"DemoDebt@1\",\n  \"status\": \"illustrative executable-method specification; no standard compliance\",\n  \"registry\": {\n    \"synthetic-note-7\": {\n      \"document\": \"synthetic disclosure NS.debt variant Acme\",\n      \"locator\": \"debt and interest paragraph\",\n      \"literal\": \"Debt 100; interest 5; fixed/floating split not disclosed\",\n      \"entity\": \"Acme\",\n      \"perimeter\": \"Acme-only\",\n      \"basis\": \"DemoDebt@1\",\n      \"concept\": \"debt_principal\",\n      \"currency\": \"USD\",\n      \"instant\": \"2025-12-31\",\n      \"precision\": \"Exact\",\n      \"amount\": {\n        \"n\": \"100\",\n        \"d\": \"1\"\n      },\n      \"accepted_reading\": \"demo-review-1\"\n    },\n    \"after-2025-close\": {\n      \"book\": \"Local\",\n      \"date\": \"2025-12-31\",\n      \"signed_balances\": {\n        \"Cash\": \"95\",\n        \"Debt\": \"-100\",\n        \"Retained\": \"5\",\n        \"InterestExpense\": \"0\"\n      },\n      \"contracts\": [\n        \"loans\"\n      ],\n      \"unpaid_interest\": \"0\"\n    },\n    \"DemoDebt.statements.v1\": {\n      \"balance_sheet\": {\n        \"cash\": \"Cash\",\n        \"debt\": \"-Debt\",\n        \"equity\": \"-Retained-current_temporary_total\"\n      },\n      \"income\": \"interest expense movements excluding closing\",\n      \"comprehensive_income\": \"profit; OCI zero\",\n      \"cash_flow\": \"interest cash settlement operating\",\n      \"equity\": \"opening equity + profit; no dividends\",\n      \"closing\": \"debit Retained / credit InterestExpense for expense balance; omit current profit from equity after closing\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"symbol_admission\": {\n    \"alpha\": {\n      \"kind\": \"HistoricalFact\",\n      \"domain\": \"[0,1]\",\n      \"evidence\": \"synthetic-note-7\",\n      \"reason\": \"Composition undisclosed\",\n      \"probability\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"currency\": {\n    \"USD\": {\n      \"scale\": 2,\n      \"posting_rounding\": \"half_even\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"DebtMix\": {\n    \"fields\": {\n      \"principal\": \"Money<book.currency>, >=0\",\n      \"fixed_fraction\": \"Real [0,1]\",\n      \"fixed_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple> >=0\",\n      \"initial_floating_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple> >=0\"\n    },\n    \"additional_terms\": {\n      \"maturity\": \"2027-12-31\",\n      \"fees\": \"0\",\n      \"currency\": \"USD\",\n      \"pay_date\": \"2026-12-31\",\n      \"accrual_period\": [\n        \"2026-01-01\",\n        \"2027-01-01\"\n      ],\n      \"year_fraction\": \"1\",\n      \"default_rule\": \"halt settlement with unpaid obligation; no hidden credit facility\"\n    },\n    \"state\": [\n      \"principal\",\n      \"fixed_principal\",\n      \"floating_principal\",\n      \"current_floating_rate\",\n      \"unpaid_interest\",\n      \"status\"\n    ],\n    \"initialization\": \"F=alpha*principal; V=(1-alpha)*principal; current_floating_rate=initial_floating_rate; unpaid_interest=0; status=performing\",\n    \"operations\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"reset\",\n        \"phase\": \"market\",\n        \"precondition\": \"date=2026-01-01; driver available\",\n        \"payload\": [\n          \"market_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"effect\": \"current_floating_rate=market_rate\",\n        \"postings\": \"none; explicit non-recognition operation\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"accrue_and_pay\",\n        \"phase\": \"settlement\",\n        \"precondition\": \"principal>=0 and cash>=rounded_interest\",\n        \"payload\": [\n          \"F\",\n          \"V\",\n          \"fixed_rate\",\n          \"current_floating_rate\",\n          \"year_fraction\"\n        ],\n        \"amount\": \"roundMoney((F*fixed_rate+V*current_floating_rate)*year_fraction,2,half_even)\",\n        \"postings\": [\n          \"Dr InterestExpense amount\",\n          \"Cr Cash amount\"\n        ],\n        \"effect\": \"interest obligation accrued and settled atomically\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"close\",\n        \"phase\": \"closing\",\n        \"precondition\": \"all required period operations committed\",\n        \"payload\": [\n          \"InterestExpense balance\"\n        ],\n        \"postings\": [\n          \"Dr Retained expense\",\n          \"Cr InterestExpense expense\"\n        ],\n        \"effect\": \"temporary account zero\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"request\": {\n    \"model\": \"BorrowingExample@1\",\n    \"evidence_view\": \"synthetic-2025-exact\",\n    \"initial_state\": \"after-2025-close\",\n    \"horizon\": [\n      \"2026-01-01\",\n      \"2027-01-01\"\n    ],\n    \"conditions\": [\n      \"allFixed\",\n      \"allFloating\"\n    ],\n    \"scenarios\": [\n      \"rateShock\"\n    ],\n    \"mode\": \"conditional\",\n    \"weight_model\": null,\n    \"reports\": [\n      \"balance_sheet\",\n      \"income\",\n      \"comprehensive_income\",\n      \"cash_flow\",\n      \"equity\",\n      \"journals\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected\": {\n    \"allFixed\": {\n      \"interest\": \"5\",\n      \"cash\": \"90\",\n      \"debt\": \"100\",\n      \"profit\": \"-5\",\n      \"equity\": \"-10\"\n    },\n    \"allFloating\": {\n      \"interest\": \"7\",\n      \"cash\": \"88\",\n      \"debt\": \"100\",\n      \"profit\": \"-7\",\n      \"equity\": \"-12\"\n    },\n    \"parent\": {\n      \"interest\": \"7-2*alpha\",\n      \"bounds\": [\n        \"5\",\n        \"7\"\n      ],\n      \"measure\": null\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '73,98p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '60,79p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,138p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '1,45p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; sed -n '95,145p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/result-review.json data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/result-review.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '73,98p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '60,79p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,138p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '1,45p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; sed -n '95,145p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/result-review.json data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/result-review.json\"","aggregated_output":"### G2. The normative language and IR contracts remain incomplete\n\nEvidence: [language scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:6),\n[core records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:84),\nand [plugin interfaces](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:117).\n\nThe grammar covers declaration forms and Appendix A supplies selected record\nsketches. There is no complete serialised expression/domain model, model-scope\nrecord, contract/economic-state schema, narrative-assertion schema, probability\nmodel, run configuration or payload definition for every result variant.\nMethods such as schedule, transition and measure are named without complete\nargument/result types. The representation names semantic hashes, capabilities\nand extension points without specifying canonical encoding, their full\nvalidation rules or required built-in function semantics.\n\nThe running program relies on DemoDebt, DebtMix, an external evidence registry,\nan opening state and reporting templates that are not fully defined in the\ndocument. It therefore cannot itself serve as a complete language conformance\nfixture.\n\nRequired repair: publish the complete Core 0 schema and reference package,\nprecise typing/context rules and function contracts, serialisation rules and\nmatched source-to-IR-to-result fixtures. Implementers need reproducible outcomes\nfor valid and invalid programs, not just agreement on names of operations.\n\n### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\nEvidence: [interpretation distinction](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:67)\nand [alternative records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:183).\n\nAn unknown fixed-rate share, two readings of a note, a permitted accounting\nelection, a measurement estimate and a future management decision are different\nuncertainties. The text recognises this, but generic symbols/choices and\nassumption provenance do not fully specify how each kind is validated,\nupdated or propagated. An unsupported treatment must not be accepted as an\nequally legitimate interpretation merely because it produces balanced entries.\n\nRequired evidence: define these distinctions in the model and review contracts,\nincluding links between dependent uncertainties. Show an admissible alternative,\nan evidence-refuted alternative and an unsupported accounting treatment.\nPreserve a possibly erroneous source assertion as evidence without silently\nendorsing its treatment. This requires no new fraud-detection product.\n\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\n\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\n\n(5 positive, 71 schema-valid negative, 2 JSON-boundary); the new accounting\ndossiers pass 17 exact/journal checks. These are bounded author evidence. The revised PDF has no serious TeX\nwarnings and received contact-sheet plus selected full-page inspection.\nThe verifier requires an author-review file and matching current-PDF render\nmanifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\nverified paper PDFs. There are 179 individual title/metadata decisions across\n194 occurrences and 72 forward queries; missing decisions stop generation.\n\nFixtures, grammar, schema and contracts are in `docs/design/fixtures` and\n`docs/design/spec`. The complete demo IR is author-entered, not generated by a\ncompiler. The new `core_semantics.py` validates the authored monetary debt\nprofile and its 17 frozen exports; unsupported sections/operations are rejected.\nIt does not prove family coverage or execute a general model. Checks evaluate\nselected IR expressions and reference financial operations; they do not certify\na production engine.\n\nSelected rule support comes from official AASB texts incorporating IAS 2,\nIAS 32 and IFRS 17. Mack's chain-ladder technical method, proofs and aggregate\nerror discussion were inspected. Sources and limits are recorded in\n`docs/design/research/standards-support.json` and\n`docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json`.\n\n## Remaining work and next justified steps\n\n1. Extend the checked debt-profile registry/reference/type validation and implement source-to-IR lowering\n   against the positive/negative cases. Schema parsing is not complete compiler\n   conformance. Preserve assumptions, context, joint symbols and branch failures.\n2. Build the bounded Northstar path and transactional replay; execute small\n   version-pinned Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger exchanges as selected.\n   Only Z3 has been exercised in this repair.\n3. Expand and independently annotate the real corpus. Apple's 121 annual pages\n   and 23 total notes are inventoried, but full semantics and incorporated\n   external documents are incomplete.\n4. Obtain full ASC authority and official/current ASBE verification. Extend\n   bank credit/prudential, insurance measurement/transition and richer hybrids\n   with primary support and complete actual fact patterns. Existing bank capital\n   assumptions are illustrative, not Basel rules. Dossiers retain source-version\n   limits and calculations; source acquisition remains internal work.\n5. After relevant internal tasks are complete, identify any consequential\n   residual questions for independent implementability/accounting review. Use\n   the unsent brief with narrow questions and a user-approved scope/cost only\n   if later commissioned. Ordinary comprehension feedback is separate and need\n   not come from a professional firm. Acceptance stays provisional while\n   internal work continues. Forecast calibration, stochastic inference and\n   performance comparisons need separate evidence plans; none was run here.\n\nG1–G18 are mapped in the result note; the wider audit is not fully closed.\nA bounded complete synthetic case must not narrow the mission. No deployment,\nexternal messaging, Git initialization or production claims were part of this\nwork. No subagents were used.\n\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"review_kind\": \"deterministic_fixed_operation_output_validation\",\n  \"checks_sha256\": \"18c55c02e5e8dc27b49fc1e8432e2be4054b09a2a869b5014d2b278f7632310d\",\n  \"scope\": \"Internal fixed-operation acceptance only; no independent model/accounting verdict.\"\n}\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"review_kind\": \"deterministic_fixed_operation_output_validation\",\n  \"checks_sha256\": \"af0cb563dcaa33f3a024051d403069b805f2460130898c89d41b80581a21724e\",\n  \"scope\": \"Internal fixed-operation acceptance only; no independent model/accounting verdict.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
